# Agent, AG-UI and GenUI rules

Source: `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md` §8; AGENT_ARCHITECTURE (PR-M3); AGUI_INTEGRATION and GENERATIVE_UI (PR-M4); PROACTIVE_INTELLIGENCE (PR-M6).

- These modules are built only from M3/M4/M6 task cards. In M0 they contain only `__init__.py` and a README.
- The model never computes a number. Every narrative number is a fact token filled by the server and checked by the verifier (DR-031).
- Model output never becomes SQL, arithmetic, HTML, URLs or executable code (SEC-05).
- Tools call the metric executor only. No tool contains SQL.
- AG-UI tool events carry sanitized summaries (metric ID, filters, row count, resultRef); never rows or SQL. Reasoning events are never forwarded.
- GenUI renders only registry kinds from validated results (`resultRef`). An invalid payload falls back to the deterministic table. No model-written code or markup.
- Detectors are deterministic, share the metric executor, and record versioned thresholds in evidence.
- AccessScope is re-checked on every read, resume, import, deep link and delivery.
